By default, the minFraud service matches devices using IP addresses. This works well in most cases, but IP-based matching can be less reliable when multiple users share the same IP address. Common scenarios include:

Shared or corporate IPs where many employees or users share a single public IP address.
Carrier-Grade NAT (CGNAT) where an ISP assigns the same public IP to many subscribers.
VPNs where multiple users route traffic through the same VPN endpoint.
Explicit device linking solves this by using a tracking_token to match devices with high confidence, independent of the IP address.